@@ -9,6 +9,18 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Passkey management
+
+Open `/devtools-times/settings/passkeys` (also linked in the header). Sign in with an existing Times account; the server verifies the password with the existing identity service and establishes an HTTP-only session. Profile names identify the account to passkey providers; the identity service's original password-login username stays unchanged.
+
+Credentials and profiles persist in SQLite at `.data/accounts.sqlite`. Run on Node 22.13 or newer. Set `ACCOUNT_DB_PATH` to a persistent volume path in deployment, and set `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` to the public origin (scheme and host, without a path or trailing slash). The RP ID is derived from that same origin for registration and all browser signals. Keep the session filesystem persistent as well; sessions expire after one day. This storage configuration is intended for a single server instance.
+
+Registration verifies the challenge, origin, RP ID and user verification before persisting public key material. Security keys are allowed. The capability-gated UI imports `webauthn-polyfills`; browsers without Signal API support can still manage credentials. Signal failures do not undo successful saves. Timestamps are epoch milliseconds; newly registered credentials have no last-used timestamp until authenticated.
+
+Provider metadata is vendored from the [community AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids/blob/main/aaguid.json). Zero and unrecognized AAGUIDs use an unknown-provider fallback. Metadata is for display only, never authorization.
+
+Run `npm run build`, `npx astro check --minimumSeverity error`, and `npm test` to verify the implementation. Browser tests use isolated fixtures and do not contact the identity service.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
